IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tn67-nouns`
IMPORT `tn67-cross-references`

-- Row il-67. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the four items: the numbers each citation names, the status of each section as the instruments read give it, both limbs, how each limb was read, and the flags.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that the citations do NOT point at in-force targets are in tn67-tests-red.l4.
-- The expected values are hand-written from NOTES.md section 6 (the answer tables), not copied from the references module.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- The numbers each citation names.
#ASSERT `the numbers the citation names` `item I1: section 50(a) cites sections 46 and 49` EQUALS LIST 46, 49
#ASSERT `the numbers the citation names` `item I2: section 51(b)(1) cites sections 45 and 46` EQUALS LIST 45, 46
#ASSERT `the numbers the citation names` `item I3: section 48 cites sections 42 to 46` EQUALS LIST 42, 43, 44, 45, 46

-- I3: the range as two integers and the set of numbers it names; the sections listed carry those numbers.
#ASSERT `item I3: the range in section 48`'s `the range starts at` EQUALS 42
#ASSERT `item I3: the range in section 48`'s `the range ends at` EQUALS 46
#ASSERT `item I3: the range in section 48`'s `the numbers the range names` EQUALS LIST 42, 43, 44, 45, 46
#ASSERT `the sections listed carry the numbers the range names` `item I3: the range in section 48`

-- The status of each section the citing words name.
#ASSERT `section 46`'s `its status` EQUALS Repealed
#ASSERT `section 45`'s `its status` EQUALS Present
#ASSERT `section 49`'s `its status` EQUALS Present
#ASSERT `section 52`'s `its status` EQUALS Present
#ASSERT `section 52A`'s `its status` EQUALS Present
#ASSERT `section 42`'s `its status` EQUALS NotChecked
#ASSERT `section 43`'s `its status` EQUALS NotChecked
#ASSERT `section 44`'s `its status` EQUALS NotChecked
#ASSERT `section 61`'s `its status` EQUALS NotChecked

-- The printed date of the instrument that repealed section 46 is the date its issue's footer prints (31.7.1980); no other section here has one.
#ASSERT `section 46`'s `the printed date of the instrument that repealed it` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 7 1980)
#ASSERT `section 45`'s `the printed date of the instrument that repealed it` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 49`'s `the printed date of the instrument that repealed it` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Both limbs hold for the four items.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I1: section 50(a) cites sections 46 and 49`
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I2: section 51(b)(1) cites sections 45 and 46`
#ASSERT `both limbs of the range citation hold` `item I3: the range in section 48`
#ASSERT `both limbs of the subsection citation hold` `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`

-- How each limb was read.
#ASSERT `item I1: section 50(a) cites sections 46 and 49`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 50(a) cites sections 46 and 49`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with later instruments examined by name (see NOTES.md)`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 51(b)(1) cites sections 45 and 46`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 51(b)(1) cites sections 45 and 46`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with later instruments examined by name (see NOTES.md)`
#ASSERT `item I3: section 48 cites sections 42 to 46`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
#ASSERT `item I3: section 48 cites sections 42 to 46`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with later instruments examined by name (see NOTES.md)`
#ASSERT `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
#ASSERT `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page image, with later instruments examined by name (see NOTES.md)`

-- I4: the subsections of section 52 as made and after item 1(2) of the amending law; the cited letter is among the first and not among the second.
#ASSERT `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`'s `the subsections of that section as made` EQUALS LIST Alef, Bet, Gimel, Dalet, He
#ASSERT `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`'s `the subsections of that section after the amending law` EQUALS LIST Alef, Bet
#ASSERT `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`'s `the subsection letter cited` EQUALS Gimel
#ASSERT `the cited subsection is among those of the section as made` `item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`

-- The flag per citation: updated by the amending law of 1982? Section 53 yes (item 3); the four items no instrument read touches.
#ASSERT `control to I4: section 53 cites sections 52, 52A and 61`'s `a later instrument read touches the citing words`
#ASSERT NOT (`item I1: section 50(a) cites sections 46 and 49`'s `a later instrument read touches the citing words`)
#ASSERT NOT (`item I2: section 51(b)(1) cites sections 45 and 46`'s `a later instrument read touches the citing words`)
#ASSERT NOT (`item I3: section 48 cites sections 42 to 46`'s `a later instrument read touches the citing words`)
#ASSERT NOT (`item I4: section 57(1) cites section 52 subsection (c)`'s `a later instrument read touches the citing words`)
